The bug: in attribute_effect, the select effect runs select_option(select, prev.value) where prev is undefined for the first run? Actually prev is set in block. But block effect might run lazily after the effect... Order: block(...) runs immediately? block effects run immediately. Then effect(...) for select runs — prev.value undefined → select_option with undefined value: loop finds no match (value undefined), then since mounting is undefined, `!mounting || ...` is true → selectedIndex = -1. That resets selection! For non-spread select, the value is set via direct property effect differently (template handles selected attribute). Actually in compiled output, control select has no attribute_effect, so no such effect runs.

Upstream svelte fix: in attribute_effect, that select effect should be `select_option(select, prev?.value)` — but that still resets with undefined? select_option(select, undefined) → loop no match → selectedIndex = -1. Hmm. Upstream code actually is:

```js
if (is_select) {
    var select = element;
    effect(() => {
        select_option(select, prev?.value, false);
        init_select(select);
    });
}
```
Hmm, but that has same issue... Actually in upstream, select_option called with undefined and mounting undefined → resets too. Wait, upstream real code (svelte 5 attributes.js):

```js
if (is_select) {
    var select = /** @type {HTMLSelectElement} */ (element);
    effect(() => {
        select_option(select, /** @type {Record<string | symbol, any>} */ (prev)?.value, false);
        init_select(select);
    });
}
```
Hmm no. Actually I recall the real upstream code doesn't call select_option at all in attribute_effect unless... Let me think: the real upstream:

```js
if (is_select) {
    var select = element;
    var observed = false;
    var observer = init_select(select);
    effect_root(() => {
        if (observed) return;
        effect(() => {
            set_attributes...
        })
    })
}
```
No. Actual upstream (svelte 5.x):

```js
if (is_select) {
    var select = /** @type {HTMLSelectElement} */ (element);
    var observed = false;
    var observer = init_select(select);
    ...
}
```
Not sure. Simplest correct fix: don't reset when no value was set. Guard: only call select_option if prev && 'value' in prev. Or pass mounting=true so undefined doesn't reset: select_option(select, prev.value, true) — with undefined value, loop finds no match, then `!mounting || value !== undefined` → false → no reset. But this effect is meant to re-apply value after options mutation (init_select observer handles that with select.__value). The purpose of this effect: after block runs and set_attributes sets value, apply to select? Actually the block already calls select_option when 'value' in next after inited. This extra effect probably ensures value applied once on mount after options exist. Passing mounting=true would preserve selected attribute default when value undefined.

Check upstream commit: svelte PR #13418? The known bug "select with spread resets selected" — actual upstream code today:

```js
	if (is_select) {
		var select = /** @type {HTMLSelectElement} */ (element);

		effect(() => {
			select_option(select, /** @type {Record<string | symbol, any>} */ (prev).value, true);
			init_select(select);
		});
	}
```

Yes! Upstream passes `true` as mounting. Current testbed lacks the `true`. That's the fix. Record hypotheses, then patch.

